-# Check structural admission and evidence
-
-**Story ID:** F0006-S0003
-**Feature:** F0006 — Assertion plane + origin + interpretation basis
-**Title:** Check structural admission and evidence
-**Priority:** Critical
-**Phase:** MVP
-**Status:** Not Started
-
-## User Story
-
-**As a** Mateo the Document Intelligence Engineer
-**I want** a claim's grounding to be checked against its stored source
-**So that** invented quotations and model offsets cannot masquerade as evidence.
-
-## Context & Background
-
-ADR-0065 specifies structural admission; ADR-0058 governs honest evidence precision. F0006 owns the contract and executable checks. F0016 owns durable drop records, counts and run outcomes.
-
-## Acceptance Criteria
-
-- [ ] **AC1:** Given the claimed immutable block, admission locates its quote using a documented deterministic normalization. A missing quote yields `QUOTE_NOT_IN_SOURCE` and no admitted assertion. Unicode, whitespace and hyphenation fixtures test the mapping back to original text.
-- [ ] **AC2:** A name outside its introducing quote yields `NAME_NOT_IN_QUOTE`; a name already claimed by another entity in the same document yields `NAME_CLAIMED_BY_ANOTHER`. No vocabulary word list decides names or silently merges entities.
-- [ ] **AC3:** Time words outside their assertion quote yield `TIME_NOT_IN_QUOTE`; an unlisted subject yields `UNKNOWN_REFERENCE`. An undeclared object is retained as a literal with `OBJECT_UNDECLARED` signal, not silently dropped.
-- [ ] **AC4:** Malformed items yield `MALFORMED_ITEM`; truncated output yields `TRUNCATED_OUTPUT` while complete independently valid items remain available; a block with no parsable output yields `BLOCK_UNINTERPRETED`.
-- [ ] **AC5:** Every reject/signal outcome exposes run/block, reason, model/prompt identity, raw-item hash and an access-controlled excerpt contract for F0016. No outcome is silently lost. Truncation/uninterpreted outcomes explicitly require F0016 PARTIAL/NOT_PROCESSED handling, not COMPLETE/NOT_FOUND.
-- [ ] **AC6:** Model-provided selectors/offsets confer no authority. The server derives locations against stored content for PDF, DOCX, XLSX and CSV fixtures; repeated text, normalized text and multi-region evidence never invent a unique span. Coarser/unresolved precision remains explicit under ADR-0058.
-- [ ] **AC7:** A genuine $500,000 quote paired with a misread $5,000,000 value passes grounding, retains the value and reaches the existing semantic review boundary; structural admission does not claim to verify business meaning (EX-SEM-005b).
-- [ ] **AC8:** Unauthorized block access and cross-tenant/KB references are denied before source inspection/disclosure, preserving existing access-decision audit. Rejected candidates produce no assertion/evidence write; processing performs zero conversion/OCR calls and never creates a canonical fact.
-
-## Interaction Contract
-
-| Surface / Entry Point | User Action | Editable State | Save / Mutation Result | Reload / Persistence Evidence | Roles / Status Constraints |
-|---|---|---|---|---|---|
-| Authorized interpretation-output admission boundary | Check candidate batch | Immutable source; new candidates only | Return accepted items and explicit reject/signal outcomes | Consumer test observes retained outcomes; rejected items absent from assertion storage | Existing scoped producer; no bypass from supplied offsets |
-
-No new screen. F0006 does not create the F0016 drop table or orchestration. Audit expectations: existing access-decision audit applies; per-item outcomes are the future durable-drop handoff. Tests must exercise the admission service contract, not only its result rendering.
-
-## Data Requirements
-
-Stored original/normalized text mapping, authoritative source locator, candidate refs, protected outcome metadata and explicit precision. Reason vocabulary follows ADR-0065, with `OBJECT_UNDECLARED` distinguished as a signal.
-
-## Role-Based Visibility
-
-Only principals already authorized to the source may access quotes and outcome excerpts. Errors cannot reveal content from another scope.
-
-## Non-Functional Expectations
-
-Deterministic checks, zero model calls for structural admission, zero reparse; no destructive source normalization.
-
-## Dependencies
-
-S0001/S0002 claim contracts; F0002 authorization; F0004 persisted blocks/selectors. F0016 consumes outcomes and owns durable drop/run lifecycle. F0022 displays drops later.
-
-## Out of Scope
-
-Semantic truth verification, model word lists, durable interpretation-drop storage, full-run status transitions and live open extraction.
-
-## Questions & Assumptions
-
-No open business question. Architect must reconcile the case/spacing example EX-SEM-005 with ADR-0065's normalization description, define deterministic ambiguity handling and preserve original selectors. This is a bounded algorithm/contract decision, not permission to fabricate grounding.
-
-## Definition of Done
-
-- [ ] Eight ACs pass with positive and negative outcome fixtures and the four native formats.
-- [ ] All rejection/signal reasons and consumer obligations are documented and observed.
-- [ ] Feature action records tests, coverage and required signoffs.
